From a4ea8daea0fb0f9c3ed0128ce53abc4e4d692906 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:51:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/26] power: supply: add Qualcomm BMS1 fuel gauge driver

Add a driver for the BMS1 fuel gauge of PM8941 and PM8226. The hardware
latches the battery open circuit voltage at power-on and whenever the
current stays low, and restarts its 36-bit coulomb counter with each
latch. The state of charge is the charge the OCV implies, from the
monitored-battery OCV tables, minus the charge counted since.

The register map and conversions follow the vendor qpnp-bms driver. The
OCV register holds a VADC code of VBAT_SNS, trimmed against the 625 mV
and 1.25 V references, not millivolts as the unmerged 2018 qcom_bms
series assumed.

Exposes capacity, charge now and since the last OCV, OCV, voltage,
current, temperature and the design limits. Unusable charge at cutoff,
FCC learning and the IADC gain trim are not implemented.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
